verify
├── malformed key, ABI, offsets, indexes or oversized assertion
│   └── reject before cryptographic validation
├── valid P256 signature but wrong RP, origin, type, challenge or crossOrigin
│   └── reject; no substring or nested-field authorization
├── missing UP/UV or inconsistent BE/BS
│   └── reject, even with a genuine signature
├── wrong public key, modified signature or high s
│   └── reject, without a raw P256 fallback
└── correct descriptor and W3C assertion
    ├── exact wire bytes produced by the TypeScript encoder
    │   └── accept the captured browser assertion; reject another challenge
    ├── native P256 unavailable
    │   └── verify using the dependency's Solidity P256 implementation
    ├── extra future client fields or zero sign counter
    │   └── accept; this stateless verifier is not the account nonce guard
    └── change EIP712 chain/account/purpose/version/nonce
        └── old assertion no longer verifies against the new digest
